--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

This binary embeds the following third-party software. All are used
unmodified, and their licenses are compatible with Apache-2.0.

Rust crates (via Cargo, see Cargo.lock for exact versions):

  axum, axum-core, hyper, http, tower      MIT
  tokio, tokio-util, tokio-stream          MIT
  serde, serde_json                        MIT OR Apache-2.0
  serde_yaml_ng                            MIT OR Apache-2.0
  rusqlite                                 MIT
  SQLite (bundled via libsqlite3-sys)      Public Domain
  rust-embed, mime_guess                   MIT
  scrypt, hmac, sha2, subtle               MIT OR Apache-2.0
  rand                                     MIT OR Apache-2.0
  clap                                     MIT OR Apache-2.0
  tracing, tracing-subscriber              MIT
  chrono                                   MIT OR Apache-2.0
  thiserror                                MIT OR Apache-2.0
  async-trait, futures-util                MIT OR Apache-2.0
  rustls (via axum-server)                 Apache-2.0 OR ISC OR MIT
  toml, hex, libc                          MIT OR Apache-2.0

Web frontend (bundled into the binary via rust-embed):

  React, React DOM                         MIT
  Ant Design, @ant-design/icons            MIT
  @tanstack/react-query                    MIT
  Vite                                     MIT

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
External programs (NOT bundled, invoked at runtime)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

  Proxmox VE (pct, pvesh, pveam, qm)       AGPL-3.0
  ttyd                                     MIT
  nftables / iproute2                      GPL-2.0

labyard invokes these as separate processes via their command-line
interfaces. It does not link against, modify, or redistribute their code,
so their licenses do not extend to labyard.
